    </div>

    <!-- Diagnostic Banner Alerts -->
    <div class="space-y-3 mb-6">
      <!-- Pathogen & Enterotoxin Status -->
      <div id="pathogenBanner" class="border border-emerald-500/30 bg-emerald-500/10 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-5 flex items-start gap-3">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m5.618-4.016A11.955 11.955 0 0112 2.944a11.955 11.955 0 01-8.618 3.04A12.02 12.02 0 003 9c0 5.591 3.824 10.29 9 11.622 5.176-1.332 9-6.03 9-11.622 0-1.042-.133-2.052-.382-3.016z" />
        </svg>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">
              {d.pathogenRiskLabel}
            </span>
            <span id="pathogenVerdictBadge" class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
              SAFE: VEGETATIVE &amp; SPORE REPLICATION SUPPRESSED
            </span>
          </div>
          <p id="pathogenVerdictText" class="text-xs text-ink/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
            Core temperature is maintained securely above 57.2°C (135°F) and 60°C (140°F), inhibiting vegetative growth and enterotoxin synthesis of Staphylococcus aureus, Bacillus cereus, and Clostridium perfringens. Note: Hot holding does NOT destroy pre-formed heat-stable enterotoxin A (SEA).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Regulatory Compliance Status -->
      <div id="complianceBanner" class="border border-blue-500/30 bg-blue-500/10 rounded-2xl p-4 sm:p-5 flex items-start gap-3">
        <svg class="w-5 h-5 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 shrink-0 mt-0.5" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
          <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12h6m-6 4h6m2 5H7a2 2 0 01-2-2V5a2 2 0 012-2h5.586a1 1 0 01.707.293l5.414 5.414a1 1 0 01.293.707V19a2 2 0 01-2 2z" />
        </svg>
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between gap-2">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300">
              {d.complianceLabel}
            </span>
            <span id="complianceVerdictBadge" class="text-xs font-mono font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">
              FDA § 3-501.16 &amp; NSF/ANSI 4 COMPLIANT
            </span>
          </div>
          <p id="complianceVerdictText" class="text-xs text-ink/80 mt-1 leading-relaxed">
            The cabinet maintains uniform temperature ≥150°F (65.6°C) throughout all pan positions with recovery times under 15 minutes, fully compliant with NSF/ANSI Standard 4 § 5.2.1 and FDA Food Code § 3-501.16(A)(1).
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Deep Dive Mechanisms & Mitigations -->
    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
      <div class="bg-surface-soft/80 border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-amber-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M13 16h-1v-4h-1m1-4h.01M21 12a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          {d.mechanismsLabel}
        </h4>
        <p id="mechanismsText" class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          High cavity relative humidity (60%–75%) maintains a narrow vapor pressure deficit (VPD < 1.0 kPa), minimizing the chemical potential driving force for surface water evaporation. In contrast, when the water pan depletes, VPD spikes above 2.5 kPa, causing rapid moisture migration from meat collagen and starch pasta matrices into the air stream.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="bg-surface-soft/80 border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
        <h4 class="text-xs font-bold text-ink uppercase tracking-wider mb-2 flex items-center gap-1.5">
          <svg class="w-4 h-4 text-emerald-500" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" viewBox="0 0 24 24">
            <path stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" stroke-width="2" d="M9 12l2 2 4-4m6 2a9 9 0 11-18 0 9 9 0 0118 0z" />
          </svg>
          {d.mitigationLabel}
        </h4>
        <p id="mitigationText" class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
          1. Refill passive water reservoir prior to reaching 4.0 hours of continuous service.<br/>
          2. Maintain thermostat setpoint at ≥150°F (65.6°C) to buffer against cold drafts from frequent door openings.<br/>
          3. Replace cracked or calcified door perimeter gaskets immediately to prevent chimney-effect cold air infiltration.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- Scientific Engineering Principles -->
<div class="bg-surface-card border border-hairline rounded-3xl p-6 sm:p-10 shadow-sm mb-12">
  <div class="mb-8">
    <h3 class="text-title-lg font-bold text-ink tracking-tight mb-2">
      {d.scienceTitle}
    </h3>
    <p class="text-body text-sm text-muted">
      {d.scienceSub}
    </p>
  </div>

  <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-2 lg:grid-cols-4 gap-4">
    <!-- Card 1 -->
    <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-amber-500/10 text-amber-600 dark:text-amber-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs mb-3">
        01
      </div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mb-1.5">Vapor Pressure Deficit (VPD)</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Evaporative surface moisture loss flux is governed by Dalton's law: J = k · (e_s(T_food) - e_a(T_air, RH)). When RH drops below 25%, the vapor pressure deficit exceeds 2.5 kPa, turning the cabinet into a commercial dehydrator.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card 2 -->
    <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-rose-500/10 text-rose-600 dark:text-rose-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs mb-3">
        02
      </div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mb-1.5">Staph Enterotoxin Stability</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Staphylococcus aureus enterotoxins (SEA, SEB) are globular proteins cross-linked by disulfide bonds. They resist 100°C for 60 minutes and 121°C for 15 minutes. Holding food at 140°F–160°F will NOT neutralize pre-formed toxins.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card 3 -->
    <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-blue-500/10 text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs mb-3">
        03
      </div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mb-1.5">NSF/ANSI Standard 4</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Section 5.2.1 mandates that hot holding cabinets maintain cavity temperatures ≥150°F (65.6°C) across all pan positions and recover to baseline within 15 minutes following a 1-minute door opening to prevent cold air stagnation.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Card 4 -->
    <div class="bg-surface-soft border border-hairline rounded-2xl p-5">
      <div class="w-8 h-8 rounded-xl bg-emerald-500/10 text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 flex items-center justify-center font-bold text-xs mb-3">
        04
      </div>
      <h4 class="text-sm font-bold text-ink mb-1.5">Gasket Chimney Convection</h4>
      <p class="text-xs text-muted leading-relaxed">
        Damaged door gaskets induce stack-effect airflow: hot humid air escapes through the top gap, drawing in cold, dry room air through the bottom perimeter. This creates a dangerous 15°F–25°F vertical temperature stratification.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

